<mjml lang="en" dir="ltr">
  <mj-head>
    <mj-include path="./partials/afiax-head.mjml" />
    <mj-title>Reset your Afiax password</mj-title>
    <mj-preview>Someone asked to reset the password for {{email}}. The link works once.</mj-preview>
  </mj-head>

  <mj-body background-color="#F1F5F9" width="600px">
    <mj-include path="./partials/afiax-header.mjml" />

    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="18px 32px 30px 32px">
      <mj-column>

        <mj-text mj-class="h1">Reset your password</mj-text>
        <mj-text>Hello{{#firstName}} {{firstName}}{{/firstName}},</mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          Someone asked to reset the password for your Afiax account, <strong style="color:#1B2A4A;">{{email}}</strong>, on the Afiax sign-in page. If that was you, choose a new password below. If it wasn't, you don't need to do anything.
        </mj-text>

        <mj-text padding="4px 0 22px 0">
          <table class="em-details" role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
            <tr><td class="k">Account</td><td class="v">{{email}}</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="k">Requested</td><td class="v">{{requestedAt}}</td></tr>
            {{#device}}<tr><td class="k">From</td><td class="v">{{device}}</td></tr>{{/device}}
            <tr><td class="k" style="border-bottom:0;">Reset link</td><td class="v" style="border-bottom:0;">Works once</td></tr>
          </table>
        </mj-text>

        <mj-text mj-class="h2">To choose a new password</mj-text>
        <mj-text padding="0 0 4px 0">
          <strong style="color:#1B2A4A;">1. Choose a new password.</strong> Use at least 8 characters. Afiax won't accept a password that has appeared in a known data leak.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-button href="{{resetUrl}}">Choose a new password</mj-button>
        <mj-text mj-class="small" padding="0 0 18px 0">
          If the button doesn't work, copy this link into your browser:<br /><span class="em-url">{{resetUrl}}</span>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          <strong style="color:#1B2A4A;">2. Sign in</strong> at <a href="{{signInUrl}}">{{signInHost}}</a> with your new password.{{#mfaEnrolled}} You'll still type the 6-digit number from your authenticator app as usual.{{/mfaEnrolled}}
        </mj-text>

        <mj-text mj-class="h2">What happens next</mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          Your old password stops working as soon as you set a new one. Setting a new password doesn't sign you out of devices where you're already signed in. To do that, open <a href="{{securityUrl}}">Security</a> in Afiax and revoke any session you don't recognise.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          If the link has already been used, or you've lost this email, choose <strong>Forgot password</strong> on the sign-in page again.
        </mj-text>

        <mj-text padding="8px 0 18px 0">
          <table class="em-help" role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
            <tr><td>
              <strong style="color:#1B2A4A;">Didn't ask for this?</strong><br />
              Your password hasn't changed, and nothing will change unless someone uses the link in this email. You can ignore it. If you keep getting these emails without asking, tell Afiax support at <a href="mailto:{{supportEmail}}">{{supportEmail}}</a>.
            </td></tr>
          </table>
        </mj-text>

      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-include path="./partials/afiax-footer.mjml" />
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
